## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/uvmap.html
- Summary (EN): Generates a UV layer in which each pixel stores its own position in UV space. Other nodes can use that layer, for example UV Sample for lookups, or Fractal Noise as a reference location.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud génère une couche UV où chaque pixel stocke sa position dans l'espace UV, réutilisable par UV Sample ou par un bruit fractal comme repère de position.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output image size and controls the metadata."]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "UV Space", "meaning": "Texture: 0 to 1 across the data window, pixels may be non-square. Image: -1 to 1 across a framed display window, with square pixels. Pixel: pixel-centre coordinates, with 0.5, 0.5 at the bottom-left pixel."}, {"name": "U Border / V Border", "meaning": "How out-of-range locations are handled: Clamp, Mirror, Wrap (repeat from the far side) or Extend (leave unchanged, useful for overscan)."}, {"name": "U Shift / V Shift", "meaning": "Offsets the location before border handling is applied."}, {"name": "U Cycles / V Cycles", "meaning": "Multiplies the location by a scale. With Wrap, this creates repeating tiles."}]

